<title>GREECE: Greek Nov building materials price index up 7.5%.</title>
<headline>Greek Nov building materials price index up 7.5%.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's building materials price index for new housing rose 7.5 percent year-on-year in November unchanged from October, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said in a statement.</p>
<p>The index was up an average 7.5 percent year-on-year in the period January-November 1996 compared to 7.3 percent and 6.7 percent in the same period in 1995 and 1994, it said.</p>
<p>					  Nov 96     Oct 96    Nov 95</p>
<p>    Month/month change (pct)     0.2	   0.4	0.3</p>
<p>    Year-on-year (pct)	     7.5	   7.5	7.4</p>
<p>    Index (1990=100)	     190.1	 189.7    176.9</p>
<p>--Margarita Sotiropoulou, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
